+- `not_applicable`: selection was reasonable but the actual change did not
+  affect that document;
+- `updated`: the same authorized work changed the document and its current
+  digest proves it;
+- `deferred_by_owner`: the unchanged document follow-up was explicitly
+  accepted by the owner and carries `owner_decision:<ref>`;
+- `conflict`: the implementation and document cannot both remain current.
+
+`conflict`, incomplete changed-path selection, an omitted disposition, or a
+path declaration that differs from Host observation blocks completion.
+`complied` and `not_applicable` never justify changing a file. Small settled
+work therefore closes with no documentation edit when current authority still
+matches.
