+# User-workflow-first hybrid policy
+
+Read this reference when the user supplies a process order, a workflow mode,
+owner checkpoints, or when risk may require a controlled route.
+
+## Precedence
+
+Apply deterministic permission, path, one-writer, risk, effect, and completion
+constraints first. Within that safe boundary use:
+
+```text
+explicit owner workflow
+→ selected Skill and Guide semantics
+→ Maestro defaults for unspecified work
+```
+
+Never silently replace or reorder owner steps. If a hard constraint conflicts,
+stop or elevate to controlled and preserve the reason and resume point.
+
+## Route contract
+
+Use Route v2. Add `--workflow-mode guided|controlled` only when the owner names
+a mode. Preserve each explicit phase with repeated `--workflow-step` in the
+original order:
+
+```text
+--workflow-step "research:Inspect current references"
+--workflow-step "work:Build one representative surface"
+--workflow-step "owner-checkpoint:Approve the representative surface"
+--workflow-step "work:Expand the approved direction"
+--workflow-step "verification:Verify rendered states"
+```
+
+Supported kinds are `research`, `work`, `owner-checkpoint`, and `verification`.
+An unprefixed step becomes `work`. Do not invent steps merely to fill the
+contract. When the owner supplies no order, keep `ordered_steps=[]` and use the
+smallest sufficient default workflow.
+
+New Route v2 and DecisionPlan objects carry `maestro_workflow_policy_v1`.
+Decision work must preserve it through enactment. A corrected route inherits
+the owner mode and ordered steps; do not use rerouting to change them.
+
+## Modes
+
+Guided is the default for ordinary low/medium work. The selected Skill decides
+whether current research, alternatives, representative artifacts, browser
+inspection, or another semantic check is useful. Guided does not remove the
+one writer, deterministic tests, or independent completion check.
+
+Controlled is required when:
+
+- the owner requests it;
+- risk is high or critical;
+- work kind is `security-sensitive`, `data-change`, or `delivery-operation`;
+- Product Design assurance mode is explicitly supplied.
+
+These are one-way floors. Never lower controlled to guided. Record the
+canonical `escalation_reasons` emitted by the route.
+
+## Product Design
+
+Always classify product-facing UI as `work_kind=user-interface` so the Product
+Design Pack can be selected. Classification alone does not activate assurance.
+For guided UI omit `--design-assurance-mode`; apply the selected Guides as
+adaptive criteria. Explicit research wording may still open research.
+
+Read `product-design-assurance.md` only when assurance is explicitly requested
+or the route is controlled. An explicit `compact|standard|system` mode activates
+controlled assurance. Controlled UI without a mode receives `standard` from
+the route compiler only after the Host confirms `work_kind=user-interface`.
+Controlled or high/critical UI without that structured classification stops
+for rerouting; never promote a lexical guess into confirmed authority. Once
+active, never weaken its packet, research, render, or preselection gates.
+
+## Runtime boundary
+
+The workflow policy is semantic input, not execution authority. Use the exact
+plan and Assignment projection. The Host must reconstruct the task contract,
+dependency projections, research and Coverage sidecars; a self-rehashed input
+does not authorize a changed workflow.
+
+Before a managed Controller start, the Skill or Host Adapter must author one
+closed step mapping. Map every executable owner step exactly once to one or
+more existing StageSpecs in owner order. Map an `owner-checkpoint` to no
+StageSpec; provide its adjacent executable step IDs plus a concrete question,
+two to eight finite options, and exactly one `resume_option_id`. These are
+task semantics and must not be generated by Core from the instruction prose.
+Core validates shape, exact coverage, no reuse, DAG happens-before, and
+digests, then projects the exact policy and mapping to each Stage.
+
+Bind an explicit owner workflow at request intake. Prefer
+`maestro orchestrate start --workflow-source <validated-route-v2.json>` so the
+exact Route plan, goal, task contract, and full policy are compared. A trusted
+direct-definition caller supplies `--workflow-policy-digest` for low/medium
+starts and also `--owner-workflow-digest` for explicit owner inputs. A
+`route-v2` source binding always requires the exact validated source and cannot
+fall back to caller-supplied digests. Its risk, intent, and task-contract
+side-effect authority must exactly match Definition risk, mutation owner, and
+mutating Stages. Owner digest alone never proves route-derived controlled
+floors. Never treat a recomputed plan ID as proof of
+owner origin. On a mapped checkpoint, present the stored Host-authored options
+and stop. While it is pending, admit only its exact DecisionResolution. Continue
+only when the exact bound receipt selects `resume_option_id`; any other option
+blocks the run.
+
+Only explicit `orchestrate start` registers `orchestration-controller-v1`.
+Generic observations keep their legacy `workflow-kernel-v1` authority; do not
+rewrite observation authority as part of this bridge.
+
+Managed plans use the configured runtime authority and checkpoint path. Record
+an Activity before an external effect. On reconciliation-required status,
+inspect the existing effect and do not blind-retry. Shadow Outcome Judge output
+is observation only. Manual outcome handling resumes from a bound owner
+DecisionResolution. Automatic activation still requires its separate evaluated
+calibration and owner approval contract.
+
+Pack evaluators return generic correction intents. Map them through an explicit
+Workflow Adapter and reject unknown domain-stage fallbacks. These runtime rules
+may block or resume owner steps but may not silently replace their order.
